      "writtenOn": "2024-01-08T18:38:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve seen memory regions described with _only_ a size (swiotlb), where it meant that the kernel should allocate it, but the opposite doesn\u0027t make sense to me; how should the kernel know how many pages to map...?\n\nAnyway, assuming that this is a valid use-case, your function doesn\u0027t detect duplicates between size-less `Reg` i.e.\n```\nlet reg \u003d Reg { addr, size: None };\nis_reg_overlap(reg, reg)\n```\nresults in\n```\naddr \u003c addr \u0026\u0026 addr \u003c addr\n```\nwhich is `false` (but shouldn\u0027t) as a result of the function dealing with semi-open intervals (as `[X;X[` is empty and therefore can\u0027t overlap with anything, not even itself).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 985,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 985,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "46ce1b33ed76187662055f134ea8aa4d56369f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
